blockads-linux for Debian and Ubuntu
====================================

The package installs everything and enables nothing. To turn protection on
(and keep it on after a reboot):

    sudo systemctl enable --now blockadsd.service blockads-update.timer blockads-update.path

Then open BlockAds from the application menu, or run `blockadsctl status`.

If DNS ever stops working, remove the firewall rules:

    sudo /usr/lib/blockads-linux/blockads-fw revert --all-backends

Removing the package stops the service and removes its rules; purging it also
deletes the settings, lists and logs in /var/lib/blockads-linux.
